`maps=true` on a target is a source map, and the golden is where it lands: an
inline `sourceMappingURL` data URI at the end of the page's script, rather
than a sidecar file the static build has nowhere to put.

The fixture was written when the option only had to not break the build --
nothing read Request.Maps -- and it passed for a second reason once something
did, since an option written in an output block was not reaching the platform
at all. Both are why the golden here is the whole page.

-- main.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output(maps=true) {
    none {
        html()
    }
}

component main node {
    text(value="hello")
}

window {
    main
}
